  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to floods in Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposal responds to a request from the Social Department of the Colombian bishops conference (SNPS), a CAFOD strategic partner, to coordinate the distribution of humanitarian aid to 5,000 families affected by the severe floods that have afflicted Colombia since October, affecting 29 of Colombia&#x2019;s 32 departments, with a total as at 23 May 2011 of three and a half million victims, including 464 dead, 566 injured and 79 missing. 

This is a follow-up request to one supported in December 2010 (COL174/1/1), since the floods have been exceptional in their severity and duration.

SNPS will provide food packages, equipment and materials for cooking, personal hygiene and cleaning, clothing and materials to rebuild houses to 5,000 families affected by the floods in 5 dioceses.  In addition SNPS will provide seeds, livestock, tools and support to re-establish livelihoods.</narrative>
  </description>
